{"version":2,"width":100,"height":36,"timestamp":1785408874,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":"bash /tmp/claude-1000/-mnt-data-Source-home-GitHub-Factory/b93ca61f-9f50-481c-932c-534ff03b0088/scratchpad/demo.sh","title":"Factory: self-host + local-model data egress (Factory#246)","env":{"SHELL":"/run/current-system/sw/bin/zsh"}}
[0.01284, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[3J"]
[0.014728, "o", "=====================================================================\r\n Factory demo -- self-host + local-model data egress    (Factory#246)\r\n=====================================================================\r\n Claim under test: a coding run on a self-hosted model, where no data\r\n left the machine.\r\n\r\n \"No data left the machine\" is a security claim. A badge that reads\r\n LOCAL is only a classification -- the software asserting its own\r\n honesty. So this take substantiates it independently: the managed\r\n inference APIs are made genuinely unreachable, so a leak FAILS the\r\n run instead of passing silently.\r\n\r\n Live on the k3d cluster \"factory\". Nothing here is reconstructed,\r\n retyped or trimmed.\r\n=====================================================================\r\n"]
[6.01851, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m1. Confirm we are not filming stale code\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.222348, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n factory get deploy pfactory -o jsonpath='{range .spec.template.spec.containers[*]}{.image}{\"\\n\"}{end}'\r\n"]
[8.068869, "o", "python:3.12-slim\r\nghcr.io/olafkfreund/pfactory:sha-5d6797e\r\n"]
[9.276436, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m gh api repos/olafkfreund/PFactory/commits/main --jq '.sha[0:7]'\r\n"]
[9.817367, "o", "\u001b]11;?\u001b\\\u001b[6n"]
[15.188755, "o", "\u001b[?1h\u001b=\r5d6797e\u001b[m\r\n\r\u001b[K\u001b[?1l\u001b>"]
[16.399135, "o", "\u001b[0;33mDeployed image tag == main. The classifier we are about to run is the shipped code.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[17.602413, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m2. The self-hosted model, as the build pod sees it\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[18.806266, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n egress-demo exec probe -- sh -c 'getent hosts host.k3d.internal; curl -s --max-time 10 http://172.18.0.1:11434/api/version; echo'\r\n"]
[20.256936, "o", "172.18.0.1        host.k3d.internal  host.k3d.internal\r\n"]
[20.26197, "o", "{\"version\":\"0.31.2\"}"]
[20.26248, "o", "\r\n"]
[21.474274, "o", "\u001b[0;33m172.18.0.1 is the k3d host gateway -- RFC-1918 private. No public address involved.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[22.677696, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n egress-demo exec probe -- sh -c 'curl -s --max-time 10 http://172.18.0.1:11434/v1/models' | jq -r '.data[].id'\r\n"]
[24.143971, "o", "qwen2.5:7b\r\nqwen2.5-coder:14b\r\ngemma4:12b\r\ngemma4:e4b\r\nnomic-embed-text:latest\r\n"]
[25.355934, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n factory get deploy aifactory -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[1].env[?(@.name==\"OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_BASE_URL\")].value}{\"\\n\"}'\r\n"]
[26.204666, "o", "http://host.k3d.internal:11434\r\n"]
[27.41336, "o", "\u001b[0;33mThat is what AIFactory is configured with today. Now AIFactory itself, enumerating those models over that endpoint:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[28.616851, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m AIF=$(kubectl --context factory -n factory get pod -o name | grep -m1 '^pod/aifactory-'); echo \"(deployment pod: $AIF)\"; kubectl --context factory -n factory exec $AIF -c aifactory -- sh -c 'curl -s --max-time 25 -H \"Authorization: Bearer $APP_API_TOKEN\" \"http://localhost:3101/api/settings/openai-compat/models?baseUrl=http%3A%2F%2Fhost.k3d.internal%3A11434\"' | jq -c .\r\n"]
[29.577771, "o", "(deployment pod: pod/aifactory-5cd59c99f4-4lsmg)\r\n"]
[30.559596, "o", "\u001b[1;39m{\u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"models\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m:\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m[\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m{\u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"name\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m:\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m\"gemma4:12b\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m}\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m{\u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"name\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m:\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m\"gemma4:e4b\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m}\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m{\u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"name\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m:\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m\"qwen2.5:7b\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m}\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m{\u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"name\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m:\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m\"qwen2.5-coder:14b\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m}\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m]\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m}\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[31.763373, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m3. PFactory's egress classifier -- the shipped code, in the deployed pod\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[32.966786, "o", "\u001b[0;33mapps/backend/byo_llm.py. Note: the pfactory pod does not carry\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[34.170886, "o", "\u001b[0;33mOPENAI_COMPATIBLE_BASE_URL, so we pass the value AIFactory uses.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[35.375171, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n factory exec deploy/pfactory -c pfactory -- sh -c 'cd /home/projects/MagesticAI/apps/backend && OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_BASE_URL=http://host.k3d.internal:11434 python byo_llm.py openai-compatible:qwen2.5-coder:14b'; echo \"exit=$?\"\r\n"]
[37.455833, "o", "{\r\n  \"model\": \"openai-compatible:qwen2.5-coder:14b\",\r\n  \"provider\": \"openai-compatible\",\r\n  \"base_url\": \"http://host.k3d.internal:11434\",\r\n  \"host\": \"host.k3d.internal\",\r\n  \"egress\": \"local\",\r\n  \"keeps_data_local\": true,\r\n  \"badge\": \"\\ud83d\\udd12 Local \\u2014 no data egress\"\r\n}\r\n\r\n🔒 Local — no data egress\r\n"]
[37.476983, "o", "exit=0\r\n"]
[38.681012, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n factory exec deploy/pfactory -c pfactory -- sh -c 'cd /home/projects/MagesticAI/apps/backend && python byo_llm.py claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929'; echo \"exit=$?\"\r\n"]
[40.67322, "o", "{\r\n  \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\r\n  \"provider\": \"claude\",\r\n  \"base_url\": null,\r\n  \"host\": null,\r\n  \"egress\": \"managed_cloud\",\r\n  \"keeps_data_local\": false,\r\n  \"badge\": \"\\u2601\\ufe0f Managed cloud \\u2014 data leaves your network\"\r\n}\r\n\r\n☁️ Managed cloud — data leaves your network\r\n"]
[40.688278, "o", "command terminated with exit code 1\r\n"]
[40.69407, "o", "exit=1\r\n"]
[41.897571, "o", "\u001b[0;33mHonest framing: that is a CLASSIFICATION of the configured endpoint, not\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[43.101274, "o", "\u001b[0;33ma measurement of the wire. It cannot prove non-egress. The rest of this\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[44.305085, "o", "\u001b[0;33mtake is the measurement.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[45.508843, "o", "\u001b[0;33m(The badge strings embed emoji glyphs, against the fleet's plain-text\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[46.712416, "o", "\u001b[0;33mstandard. Shown unedited because it is real product output; PFactory\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[47.915736, "o", "\u001b[0;33missue filed to replace them.)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[49.119455, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m4. Baseline -- with no egress policy, this pod reaches every managed model API\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[50.322839, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n egress-demo get netpol\r\n"]
[51.170541, "o", "No resources found in egress-demo namespace.\r\n"]
[52.379174, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n egress-demo exec probe -- sh -c 'for h in https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages https://api.openai.com/v1/models https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models; do printf \"%-58s \" \"$h\"; curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"http=%{http_code} connect=%{time_connect}s\\n\" --max-time 10 \"$h\" || echo \"curl exit=$?\"; done'\r\n"]
[53.909285, "o", "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages                      "]
[54.078319, "o", "http=405 connect=0.084525s\r\n"]
[54.080677, "o", "https://api.openai.com/v1/models                           "]
[54.419552, "o", "http=401 connect=0.066891s\r\n"]
[54.422249, "o", "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models    "]
[54.62798, "o", "http=403 connect=0.099689s\r\n"]
[55.840924, "o", "\u001b[0;33m405 / 401 / 400-class answers mean TCP, TLS and HTTP all completed.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[57.044452, "o", "\u001b[0;33mAnthropic, OpenAI and Google are all reachable from here right now.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[58.247904, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m5. Make them genuinely unreachable -- default-deny egress, fail-closed\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[59.451812, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m cat /tmp/claude-1000/-mnt-data-Source-home-GitHub-Factory/b93ca61f-9f50-481c-932c-534ff03b0088/scratchpad/netpol.yaml\r\n"]
[59.956998, "o", "apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\r\nkind: NetworkPolicy\r\nmetadata:\r\n  name: local-model-only\r\n  namespace: egress-demo\r\nspec:\r\n  podSelector:\r\n    matchLabels:\r\n      app: probe\r\n  policyTypes:\r\n    - Egress\r\n  egress:\r\n    # DNS only, to the in-cluster resolver.\r\n    - to:\r\n        - namespaceSelector: {}\r\n          podSelector:\r\n            matchLabels:\r\n              k8s-app: kube-dns\r\n      ports:\r\n        - protocol: UDP\r\n          port: 53\r\n        - protocol: TCP\r\n          port: 53\r\n    # The self-hosted Ollama endpoint on the host gateway. Nothing else.\r\n    - to:\r\n        - ipBlock:\r\n            cidr: 172.18.0.1/32\r\n      ports:\r\n        - protocol: TCP\r\n          port: 11434\r\n"]
[61.160765, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory apply -f /tmp/claude-1000/-mnt-data-Source-home-GitHub-Factory/b93ca61f-9f50-481c-932c-534ff03b0088/scratchpad/netpol.yaml\r\n"]
[62.833138, "o", "networkpolicy.networking.k8s.io/local-model-only created\r\n"]
[67.045904, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n egress-demo exec probe -- sh -c 'for h in https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages https://api.openai.com/v1/models https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models; do printf \"%-58s \" \"$h\"; curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"http=%{http_code}\\n\" --max-time 10 \"$h\" || echo \"BLOCKED (curl exit=$?)\"; done; printf \"%-58s \" \"http://172.18.0.1:11434/api/version\"; curl -s --max-time 10 http://172.18.0.1:11434/api/version; echo'\r\n"]
[68.503396, "o", "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages                      "]
[68.510975, "o", "http=000\r\n"]
[68.511207, "o", "BLOCKED (curl exit=7)\r\nhttps://api.openai.com/v1/models                           "]
[68.518444, "o", "http=000\r\n"]
[68.518785, "o", "BLOCKED (curl exit=7)\r\nhttps://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models    "]
[74.468704, "o", "http=000\r\n"]
[74.468996, "o", "BLOCKED (curl exit=7)\r\nhttp://172.18.0.1:11434/api/version                        "]
[74.474858, "o", "{\"version\":\"0.31.2\"}"]
[74.475251, "o", "\r\n"]
[75.686035, "o", "\u001b[0;33mAll three managed inference APIs refused. The local model is still reachable.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[76.889674, "o", "\u001b[0;33mThis is the point of the whole exercise: from here on, a leak to a managed\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[78.092852, "o", "\u001b[0;33mmodel API cannot succeed quietly -- it FAILS the run.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[79.296396, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m6. The coding stage, on the local model, inside that policy\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[80.500146, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m sed -n '1,12p' /tmp/claude-1000/-mnt-data-Source-home-GitHub-Factory/b93ca61f-9f50-481c-932c-534ff03b0088/scratchpad/codegen.py\r\n"]
[81.006159, "o", "#!/usr/bin/env python3\r\n\"\"\"Coding-stage model call, provider-agnostic.\r\n\r\nExactly one thing changes between a local run and a cloud run: MODEL and\r\nBASE_URL. The wire protocol (OpenAI-compatible /v1/chat/completions) and this\r\nfile are identical either way. Run under the egress NetworkPolicy: if the\r\nconfigured endpoint is not the private local one, the call cannot connect.\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\nimport json\r\nimport os\r\nimport sys\r\n"]
[82.209606, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n egress-demo exec probe -- sh -c 'MODEL=qwen2.5-coder:14b BASE_URL=http://172.18.0.1:11434 python3 /tmp/codegen.py >/tmp/run.log 2>&1 & sleep 3; echo \"-- established TCP sockets in this pod while the model call is in flight --\"; ss -tn state established; wait; echo; echo \"-- result --\"; cat /tmp/run.log'\r\n"]
[86.65123, "o", "-- established TCP sockets in this pod while the model call is in flight --\r\n"]
[86.673295, "o", "Recv-Q Send-Q Local Address:Port  Peer Address:Port\r\n0      0         10.42.1.82:43238   172.18.0.1:11434\r\n"]
[92.744164, "o", "\r\n-- result --\r\nmodel      : qwen2.5-coder:14b\r\nendpoint   : http://172.18.0.1:11434/v1/chat/completions\r\nelapsed    : 8.8s\r\ntokens     : prompt=118 completion=269\r\nRESULT     : code generated\r\n"]
[93.956795, "o", "\u001b[0;33mOne socket. Peer 172.18.0.1:11434 -- private, on this box. Nothing else.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[95.160621, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n egress-demo exec probe -- cat /tmp/generated.py\r\n"]
[96.613802, "o", "import re\r\n\r\ndef parse_duration(text: str) -> int:\r\n    if not text:\r\n        raise ValueError(\"Empty input\")\r\n    \r\n    pattern = r\"(\\d+h)?(\\d+m)?(\\d+s)?\"\r\n    match = re.match(pattern, text)\r\n    \r\n    if not match:\r\n        raise ValueError(\"Unparseable input\")\r\n    \r\n    hours = int(match.group(1)[:-1]) if match.group(1) else 0\r\n    minutes = int(match.group(2)[:-1]) if match.group(2) else 0\r\n    seconds = int(match.group(3)[:-1]) if match.group(3) else 0\r\n    \r\n    return hours * 3600 + minutes * 60 + seconds\r\n\r\ndef test_parse_duration():\r\n    assert parse_duration(\"1h30m\") == 5400\r\n    assert parse_duration(\"45s\") == 45\r\n    assert parse_duration(\"2h\") == 7200\r\n    assert parse_duration(\"90m\") == 5400\r\n    assert parse_duration(\"\") == ValueError\r\n    assert parse_duration(\"abc\") == ValueError\r\n\r\n# Uncomment the following lines to run the tests\r\n# if __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n#     test_parse_duration()\r\n"]
[97.824061, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m7. Verify the generated code -- also entirely local\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[99.028383, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n egress-demo exec probe -- sh -c 'cd /tmp && python3 -c \"import generated; generated.test_parse_duration(); print(\\\"tests passed\\\")\"'; echo \"verify exit=$?\"\r\n"]
[100.524268, "o", "Traceback (most recent call last):\r\n"]
[100.524622, "o", "  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\r\n    import generated; generated.test_parse_duration(); print(\"tests passed\")\r\n                      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^\r\n  File \"/tmp/generated.py\", line 24, in test_parse_duration\r\n    assert parse_duration(\"\") == ValueError\r\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^\r\n  File \"/tmp/generated.py\", line 5, in parse_duration\r\n    raise ValueError(\"Empty input\")\r\n"]
[100.524659, "o", "ValueError: Empty input\r\n"]
[100.534916, "o", "command terminated with exit code 1\r\n"]
[100.540753, "o", "verify exit=1\r\n"]
[101.744475, "o", "\u001b[0;33mThat is the real result, shown unedited. For the error cases the local 14B\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[102.948181, "o", "\u001b[0;33mmodel asserted on the RETURN VALUE of parse_duration instead of asserting\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[104.152119, "o", "\u001b[0;33mthat the call raises -- so the test blows up on the first error case.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[105.356319, "o", "\u001b[0;33mVerify caught it. Quality parity with a frontier model is NOT the claim\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[106.559647, "o", "\u001b[0;33mbeing made here. The claim is that it ran and nothing egressed.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[107.763171, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m8. Provider swap -- change only the endpoint string\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[108.966831, "o", "\u001b[0;33mSame file, same OpenAI-compatible wire protocol. Only MODEL and BASE_URL differ.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[110.170402, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n egress-demo exec probe -- sh -c 'MODEL=gpt-4o-mini BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com python3 /tmp/codegen.py'; echo \"exit=$?\"\r\n"]
[111.697696, "o", "model      : gpt-4o-mini\r\nendpoint   : https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions\r\n"]
[111.771456, "o", "elapsed    : 0.1s\r\nRESULT     : COULD NOT CONNECT -- <urlopen error [Errno 111] Connection refused>\r\n            : no bytes left this pod.\r\n"]
[111.786431, "o", "command terminated with exit code 3\r\n"]
[111.791745, "o", "exit=3\r\n"]
[112.995199, "o", "\u001b[0;33mUnder the policy the cloud path cannot connect. Now remove the policy and\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[114.198753, "o", "\u001b[0;33mre-run the identical command, to show the policy is what makes the difference:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[115.401963, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n egress-demo delete netpol local-model-only\r\n"]
[116.530184, "o", "networkpolicy.networking.k8s.io \"local-model-only\" deleted from egress-demo namespace\r\n"]
[121.021448, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubectl --context factory -n egress-demo exec probe -- sh -c 'MODEL=gpt-4o-mini BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com python3 /tmp/codegen.py'; echo \"exit=$?\"\r\n"]
[122.546679, "o", "model      : gpt-4o-mini\r\nendpoint   : https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions\r\n"]
[123.184267, "o", "elapsed    : 0.6s\r\nRESULT     : CONNECTED -- remote server answered HTTP 401\r\n            : data reached the far end. This IS egress.\r\n"]
[123.200261, "o", "command terminated with exit code 2\r\n"]
[123.205473, "o", "exit=2\r\n"]
[124.409415, "o", "\u001b[0;33mHTTP 401 from OpenAI. We hold no key, so the generation cannot complete --\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[125.61296, "o", "\u001b[0;33mbut the connection completed and our prompt reached a third party. That is\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[126.816825, "o", "\u001b[0;33megress, measured, and it is what the local run demonstrably did not do.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[128.020431, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m9. What this take proves, and what it does not\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[129.225548, "o", "  PROVEN, by measurement:\r\n    - The coding-stage model call went to 172.18.0.1:11434, a private\r\n      address on this machine. One socket, no others (ss, in the pod netns).\r\n    - While it ran, api.anthropic.com, api.openai.com and\r\n      generativelanguage.googleapis.com were all unreachable from that pod\r\n      (connection refused). A leak to a managed model API would have FAILED\r\n      the run, not passed silently.\r\n    - The same code, pointed at api.openai.com, fails closed with the policy\r\n      on and connects (HTTP 401) with it off. The control is doing the work.\r\n    - Verify ran locally and caught a genuine defect in the local model's\r\n      output.\r\n\r\n  NOT PROVEN by this take:\r\n    - The LOCAL badge from byo_llm.py is a classification of the configured\r\n      endpoint. It is not, and cannot be, a measurement. Do not read it as one.\r\n    - The factory namespace has NO egress NetworkPolicy today. The policy\r\n      shown here was applied to an isolated demo namespace for this run.\r\n      The fleet's real build pods are not yet fail-closed.\r\n    - This is the coding and verify stage of one task, not a full four-service\r\n      PARR run driven through PFactory, AIFactory and TFactory on local models.\r\n"]
[137.230013, "x", "0"]
